### Checklist

- [ ] Confirmed that `cargo run-checks` has been executed.
- [ ] Made sure the book is up to date with changes in this PR.

> `cargo run-checks` tests with `Flex` by default. Use `cargo run-checks --backend <backend>` when
> targeting another backend. Consider running additional tests relevant to the crates changed.

### Changes

Replaced declarative dispatch macros with `#[backend_dispatch]`, sharing routing/logic with `#[backend_extension]`.

Example usage:
```rust
#[backend_dispatch]
impl ModuleOps<Self> for Dispatch {
    fn batch_norm(
        x: FloatTensor<Self>,
        gamma: FloatTensor<Self>,
        beta: FloatTensor<Self>,
        mean: FloatTensor<Self>,
        variance: FloatTensor<Self>,
        epsilon: f64,
    ) -> FloatTensor<Self> {
        B::batch_norm(x, gamma, beta, mean, variance, epsilon)
    }
}
```

Replaced the implicit autodiff checkpointing field contract with an explicit `DispatchAutodiffContext`.
```rust
pub struct DispatchTensor {
    /// Tensor kind primitive.
    pub kind: DispatchTensorKind,
    /// Autodiff backend association for this tensor.
    pub autodiff: DispatchAutodiffContext,
}

pub enum DispatchAutodiffContext {
    /// Route the tensor through its concrete backend.
    #[default]
    Disabled,
    /// Associate the tensor with an autodiff backend using the given strategy.
    Enabled(GradientCheckpointingStrategy),
}
```

This should really improve maintainability and robustness by replacing ~1.1k lines of declarative macros with a shared, typed and testable routing dispatch logic used by the proc-macros.

### Testing

Additional behavioral coverage
